FIX FE BACKGROUND FILL: FUN_00411e0c's prim is ARG 1, not ARG 3 (patch-480 frame miscount)

FUN_00411e0c @0x411e0c (flat-tile fill, primfuncs[0x60], the FE full-screen
background clear) has a 4-push prologue:

  411e0c: push ebx; push esi; push edi; push ebp
  411e10: mov ebp,esp            ; [ebp+0x10] = RETURN ADDRESS
  411e15: mov edx,[ebp+0x14]     ; = ARG 1 = the prim (DrawOTag pushes it last)

Patch 480 read [ebp+0x14] as "the third argument" (it counted a standard
enter-style frame, missing that the four pushes shift the arg base to +0x14)
and moved the prim to arg 3 of the normalized 3-arg handler signature. DrawOTag
dispatches (prim, walkpos, node), so the handler decoded the OT NODE address as
its rect: h parsed <= 0 -> zero pixels painted. Effect: the FE's per-frame
full-screen f0 background fill (Draw_Tile prim @0x93fff0, type 0x60, inserted
at OT[1023] by FUN_00451a6c) NEVER painted; races were unaffected (no type-0x60
prims in race OTs). Visible: FE menu edge columns x in {0,1,638,639} kept boot
residue instead of ref's f0 -- the last 1688/307200 px of the FE-menu-vs-ref
compare (interior was already exact). Verified against the reference: ref's
menu edges are f0 precisely because this fill paints every FE frame.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 void __cdecl FUN_00411a04(int param_1,int _p2,int _p3);
 void __cdecl FUN_00411b34(int param_1,int _p2,int _p3);
 void __cdecl FUN_00411c78(int param_1,int _p2,int _p3);
-void FUN_00411e0c(int _p1,int _p2,int param_1);
+void FUN_00411e0c(int param_1,int _p2,int _p3);
 void __cdecl FUN_00411ebc(int *param_1,undefined *param_2);
 void __cdecl FUN_0041243c(int *param_1,undefined *param_2);
 void __cdecl FUN_00412694(int param_1,int _ot_b,int _ot_c);  /* patch 765: call_indirect signature normalization */
@@ -2213,9 +2213,15 @@
 
 /* ===== FUN_00411e0c @ 00411e0c ===== */
 
-void FUN_00411e0c(int _p1,int _p2,int param_1)
+void FUN_00411e0c(int param_1,int _p2,int _p3)
 
 {
+  /* asm frame: push ebx/esi/edi/ebp; mov ebp,esp -> [ebp+0x10]=ret, [ebp+0x14]=ARG 1.
+     Patch 480 mapped [ebp+0x14] to arg 3 (miscounted the four prologue pushes); DrawOTag
+     pushes (node, walkpos, prim-LAST) so the handler read the OT-walk NODE as its rect ->
+     h decoded <=0 -> the FE full-screen f0 background fill (Draw_Tile prim @0x93fff0,
+     type 0x60) never painted; FE menu edge columns x{0,1,638,639} kept boot residue
+     (1688 px vs ref). Prim = ARG 1, matching every other normalized handler. */
   int iVar1;
   int iVar2;
   int iVar3;
